{{also|Testudo}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|la|en}} {{lena}}, from {{term|testa|lang=la||the shell of shellfish, or of testaceous animals}}. See {{term|Testudo|lang=en||tortoise genus}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|testudoes|testudines}}

# {{context|historical|Roman antiquity|lang=en}} A [[shelter]] formed by a body of [[troop]]s by holding their [[shield]]s or [[target]]s close together over their heads.
# {{context|music|lang=en}} A kind of [[lyre]]; so called in allusion to the lyre of Mercury, fabled to have been made of the shell of a tortoise.

{{Webster 1913}}

